From a30866b4b433dfe964ee32b27381b3b41295ee66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Developer 2 (Client & Delivery)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 11:15:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(vitals): install Chromium instead of pointing at a path
 the runner does not have
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unit: F-2 guard follow-up (Auditor-accepted, VERIFIED on run 33746276312).
On PR #137 the first real run of d2-web-vitals.yml failed at the F-2 guard:
"the harness did not run: chromium would not launch: Executable doesn't exist
at /opt/pw-browsers/chromium_headless_shell-1234/...". Zero measured samples.

Cause, not symptom: the job pinned PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH to /opt/pw-browsers
— a directory that exists in the sandbox this workflow was written in and not
on a GitHub runner — and never installed a browser at all. The comment beside
that variable ("nothing new is installed here") asserted the bug as a fact;
Standing Rule 21, so it is deleted with the line rather than left to mislead.

Fix: delete the pin so Playwright uses its default cache, and adopt ui-gate.yml's
existing block verbatim — actions/cache@v4 on ~/.cache/ms-playwright, then
`npx playwright install chromium` with a three-attempt retry and a hard error
if all three fail. Its two YAML steps are byte-identical to ui-gate.yml's; only
the surrounding comment differs, and it carries the same reasons (cache, retry,
no --with-deps because apt hung builds 1107 and 1109).

No dependency change: Playwright is already a devDependency and the Phase 0
window stays closed. No `${{ }}` inside any run: block (F-47). The guard is not
weakened — a browser that still cannot install fails the job, which is the whole
point of the guard that caught this.

Proved locally on this head, 2026-09-03T11:14Z: with the pin removed,
`npx playwright install chromium` lands chromium-1234 and
chromium_headless_shell-1234 in ~/.cache/ms-playwright — exactly the binary the
failing run could not find — and the guard's own node script, run verbatim
against the harness output, prints "6 measured sample(s) … the harness ran" and
exits 0. Before: run 33746276312, guard exit 1, 0 samples.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017fdB5mybV9pixsM7n9b9Tf
---
 .github/workflows/d2-web-vitals.yml | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/d2-web-vitals.yml b/.github/workflows/d2-web-vitals.yml
index abd4c49..bb9e17a 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/d2-web-vitals.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/d2-web-vitals.yml
@@ -97,11 +97,6 @@ jobs:
       VITE_CDN_HOST: cdn-staging.50mmretina.com
       VITE_SITE_ORIGIN: https://staging.50mmretina.com

-      # Where this runner keeps its browsers. Playwright is already a
-      # devDependency of this repository; nothing new is installed here, and the
-      # Phase 0 dependency window is closed.
-      PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH: /opt/pw-browsers
-
       EVIDENCE_DIR: docs/evidence/d2/baseline
       # Home first, then the two heaviest surfaces a member actually opens.
       # A route that does not exist still measures — the SPA serves index.html
@@ -121,6 +116,56 @@ jobs:
       - name: Clean install
         run: npm ci --no-audit --no-fund

+      # ⚠ THE F-2 GUARD CAUGHT THIS ON ITS FIRST REAL RUN, 2026-09-03.
+      #
+      # Run 33746276312 (PR #137) failed at "The harness measured something"
+      # with: chromium would not launch: Executable doesn't exist at
+      # /opt/pw-browsers/chromium_headless_shell-1234/... . Two faults, one
+      # cause: this job set PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH to /opt/pw-browsers — a
+      # directory that exists in the sandbox this workflow was written in and
+      # NOT on a GitHub runner — and it never installed a browser at all. The
+      # comment beside that variable said "nothing new is installed here",
+      # which was true and was the bug. Both are gone: the pin is deleted, so
+      # Playwright uses its default cache, and the browser is installed here.
+      #
+      # This is `ui-gate.yml`'s block, deliberately unchanged rather than a
+      # second way of doing the same thing — including the reasons it has the
+      # shape it has:
+      #
+      #   * CACHED, because the download is the slow part on a repeat run.
+      #   * RETRIED three times, because build 1107 died on Ubuntu's mirror,
+      #     not on anything wrong with this repository.
+      #   * NO `--with-deps`, and that is the fix, not an omission: `--with-deps`
+      #     runs apt, apt hung builds 1107 and 1109 past the job budget, and it
+      #     does not fail fast, so the retry never reached attempt two. The
+      #     GitHub ubuntu image already ships the shared libraries Chromium
+      #     needs.
+      #   * AND IF IT STILL CANNOT INSTALL, THIS FAILS. A harness that cannot
+      #     launch a browser measures nothing, and nothing is not a value —
+      #     which is precisely what the F-2 guard downstream exists to say.
+      #
+      # No dependency change: Playwright is already a devDependency, and the
+      # Phase 0 dependency window stays closed.
+      - name: Cache the Playwright browser
+        uses: actions/cache@v4
+        with:
+          path: ~/.cache/ms-playwright
+          key: playwright-chromium-${{ hashFiles('package-lock.json') }}
+
+      - name: Install Chromium for Playwright
+        run: |
+          set -uo pipefail
+          for attempt in 1 2 3; do
+            if npx playwright install chromium; then
+              echo "Chromium ready (attempt ${attempt})."
+              exit 0
+            fi
+            echo "::warning::Chromium download attempt ${attempt} failed; retrying."
+            sleep $((attempt * 15))
+          done
+          echo "::error::Chromium could not be downloaded after 3 attempts."
+          exit 1
+
       - name: Build the staging lane
         run: npm run build

